  "title": "Police Use Tear Gas on Young Indians as Government Jobs Protest Escalates",
  "summary": "Demonstrators in Jharkhand accused authorities of failing to address irregularities in exams for sought-after civil service jobs, leading to a clash with police as the protest escalated into a march on the state legislature. Police deployed teargas and batons to disperse the crowd, while protesters expressed frustration over the system’s flaws.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The government’s job recruitment process has been criticized for irregularities, with many young individuals seeking government jobs in the field of education and civil service.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Demonstrators clashed with police in Jharkhand, one of India’s poorest states, as a weeks-long protest over recruitment issues intensified.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Police used teargas and batons to disperse the crowd, and some protesters responded by dancing and cheering.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The protests have led to a movement for an overhaul of the education and job recruitment system in India.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
