    {
      "title": "Police use teargas on young Indians as government jobs protest escalates",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/10/indian-police-use-force-to-disperse-youth-protesters-calling-for-exam-overhaul",
      "description": "<p>Demonstrators accuse authorities of failing to tackle irregularities in exams for sought-after civil service jobs</p><p>Thousands of angry young job-seekers clashed with police in Jharkhand, one of India’s poorest states, on Monday as a weeks-long protest over alleged irregularities in recruitment drives for coveted government jobs escalated into a march on the state legislature.</p><p>Police fired water cannon and teargas and swung batons as they tried to stop flag-waving demonstrators from clambering over barricades and surging towards the assembly in Ranchi, the state capital. Some of the protesters responded by dancing and cheering as jets of water drenched the crowd.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/10/indian-police-use-force-to-disperse-youth-protesters-calling-for-exam-overhaul\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-10T17:16:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Police in India Use Tear Gas to Break Youth Protest",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/10/world/asia/police-india-protest-jharkhand-jobs.html",
      "description": "Thousands of protesters in the eastern state of Jharkhand claim irregularities in qualifying exams for government jobs and are demanding an overhaul of the system.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-08-10T19:30:08"
    }
